#taxon[Idea]
#title[Generating Type of Species]

We can categorify the generating functions very similarly:

$
  G_F (X) :-= sum_(A: "FinSet") F(A) xx (A -> X)
$

Edit: Yes, this is exactly what they do in #local("00G5")[From Finite Sets to Feynman Diagrams].
see #local("00G4")[Exponential Generating Type].

